					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/uncle-nicolini" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3487700); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3487700&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200711" alt="Uncle Nicolini" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3487700)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/uncle-nicolini" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3487700); return false;" >Uncle Nicolini</a></span> <span class="odate time_1534871034 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Aug 2018 17:03</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3920604">
									

<p>As much as I enjoy the concept, the clinical tone isn't quite there and there are too many errors to warrant an upvote from me right now.</p>
<p>But for real though, predatory pianos are awesome.</p>
<p>EDIT: I'll clip some bits that stand out the most shortly.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Any music played by SCP-4088 is to be recorded and sent to Head Researcher Zarakolv</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missing a full stop.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4088 is mobile, <span style="text-decoration: underline;">moving around</span></p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>then will lurch towards the prey and attempt to slam its lid shut on the prey. SCP-4088 will continue to do this until the prey is deceased, then it will drop the prey into its interior where the body will disappear.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>the word 'prey' is used four times with less than ten words between each use, which creates a semantic sensation.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The way that this occurs is currently unknown, as it only appears to occur when no humans are observing the room though any means</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The way that SCP-4088-1 is able to support SCP-4088</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The subject that is standing under SCP-4088 when it is falling will not attempt to retreat, and only looks up at SCP-4088 with a terrified expression. SCP-4088 falling onto the subject almost always ends in death,</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>This appears to be the song SCP-4088 uses the most to draw in prey.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Now that I read this again, there's an awful lot of semantic sensation on top of the tonal issues. It also feels as if the 'amounts played' part of the table doesn't add much as we can infer how often it would be heard to be playing the songs based on its established behaviors as a predator.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

