			<div class="content" id="post-content-3922308">
									

<p>I will probably regret coming down so hard here&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>&#8230;but this is sub-draft-level writing. And I <em>want</em> to like this because I am a fan of classical music, pianos, and Mr. Joel.</p>
<p>In addition to the errors and issues Uncle Nic pointed out&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4088 is mobile, bending it's legs</p>
</blockquote>
<p>its, not it's</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4088-1's anomalous properties only manifest when left in a closed room with SCP-4088 and not observed&#8230;The way that this occurs is currently unknown, as this behavior only manifests when no humans are observing the room though any means.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is inexcusably redundant, you say the exact same thing two sentences apart from one another.</p>
<p>Additional instances of repeated words:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4088 then will wait wait until</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The damage caused to the subject will almost always end in death, with the cause</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>to regrow the length of its rope through unknown means, at a rate of 2 meters regrown an hour.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Both visually and compositionally, the second paragraph needs to be split into two; it is too long as is.</p>
<p>The installment of the victim's sudden inability to run away, left instead in helplessness to only look up with a scared expression introduces a strikingly powerful psychological/neuro/musculoskeletal component to this anomaly's abilities, yet it is never detailed and is only placed compositionally to ensure that people die. It also doesn't make any sense that it isn't used by the anomaly at other times. You've already mentioned that the piano can move at remarkable speed, why can't it simply drop at similar speeds too?</p>
<p>I'm sorry, I either upvote or novote 98% of the time, but I just have to downvote this.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I do love the imagery of a predatorily-toothed piano.</p>

